  "strategy_effect_null": "Unpaired CIs overlap (point estimates span 32%), but the paired per-doc test is decisive: a_random < c_balanced (mean \u0394\u03ba' = -0.00010, Bonferroni CI [-0.00011, -0.00008], 32/32 docs) \u2014 the ranking is significant, but the point-estimate spread is only 16% (within individual CI widths): V_new choice matters for ranking, not for a large effect. Full pair-wise results: res[paired_tests].",
  "verdict": "surgery_approximate_bottom_svs,rank_regime_moderate_178,dryrun_kappa_min_0.0003",
  "limitations": [
    "Sentinel split (E-34, 50.7%) NOT computable from exp27b cache: P128 stores probability-normalized top-128 masses (sum=1), raw logit masses absent. Body-subset is the canonical choice; r_eff(body) is an upper bound on r_eff(body_non_sentinel).",
    "Dry-run \u03ba' uses cached \u00fb_t (base model) \u2014 the real E-39c model has changed embed_tokens (tied weights), so \u00fb_t of the edited model differs; \u03ba' here is a PREVIEW, not the E-39c measurement. The verdict dryrun_kappa_min_* must not be read as an E-39c result.",
    "Spec \u00a71.4 asked for \u03c1_noise as the contamination diagnostic; the dry-run \u03ba' is reported instead/alongside as a more direct metric (\u03c1_noise_u_obs_overlap_mean is also reported per strategy).",
    "Strategy (b) principal = QR(P_pool\u00b7V_top16(M_K)); if M_K top-16 has a large U_obs component the projection loses rank and (b) \u2248 (a) \u2014 see v_a_v_b_projector_frobenius_dist, v_a_v_b_max_principal_angle_deg and the qr_rank_ok flags.",
    "strategy effect: point estimates span 32% (0.00030..0.00039); CIs overlap, and the spread is within individual bootstrap CI widths (~26-34%). M_rest is shared by all three strategies, so a real difference can only come from the V_new \u2194 M_rest coupling \u2014 but at N=32 we cannot establish that the spread is real, and the M_rest-dominates hypothesis is also not confirmed. Paired per-doc test below.",
    "paired per-doc test (a_random \u2212 b_principal, n=32 pairs, Bonferroni \u03b1 = 0.05/3 \u2248 0.0167 two-sided, 95%\u219298.33% CI): mean \u0394\u03ba' = -0.00008, CI [-0.00009, -0.00007], 32/32 docs lower for a_random. a_random < b_principal is statistically significant (CI excludes 0, consistent per-doc direction) \u2014 the difference is real, but small relative to the ~16% overall point-estimate spread: V_new choice matters for ranking, not for a large effect.",
    "paired per-doc test (a_random \u2212 c_balanced, n=32 pairs, Bonferroni \u03b1 = 0.05/3 \u2248 0.0167 two-sided, 95%\u219298.33% CI): mean \u0394\u03ba' = -0.00010, CI [-0.00011, -0.00008], 32/32 docs lower for a_random. a_random < c_balanced is statistically significant (CI excludes 0, consistent per-doc direction) \u2014 the difference is real, but small relative to the ~16% overall point-estimate spread: V_new choice matters for ranking, not for a large effect.",
